G4521.def:
**σάββατον**, -ου, τό (Aram. שַׁבָּתָא, transliterated σάββατα, and this being mistaken for a pl., the sing. σάββατον was formed from it), and σάββατα, -ων, τά
[in LXX for שַׁבָּת, שַׁבָּתוֹן ;]
1. the seventh day of the week, the sabbath
(a) the sing. form -ον, τὸ σ.: [[Mat.12.8|Mat.12:8]], [[Mrk.2.27|Mrk.2:27]], [[Luk.6.5|Luk.6:5]], al.; ἡ ἡμέρα τοῦ σ. (in LXX, [[Exo.20.8|Exo.20:8]], al., usually τῶν σ., see infr.), [[Luk.13.16; 14.5|Luk.13:16 14:5]]; ὁδὸς σαββάτου, [[Act.1.12|Act.1:12]] (cf. [[Mat.24.29|Mat.24:29]]); dative, of time (τῷ) σ., [[Luk.6.9; 14.1|Luk.6:9 14:1]]; ἐν (τῷ) σ., [[Mat.12.2|Mat.12:2]], [[Luk.6.7|Luk.6:7]], [[Jhn.5.16|Jhn.5:16]], al.; accusative, of duration, τὸ σ., [[Luk.23.56|Luk.23:56]] κατὰ πᾶν σ., [[Act.13.27; 15.21; 18.4|Act.13:27 15:21 18:4]]; pl., σ. τρία, [[Act.17.2|Act.17:2]] R, txt. (but see infr.);
(b) as most frequently in LXX (see Swete, _Mk._, 17; Thackeray, _Gr._, 35) the pl. form, τὰ σ. (see supr. on the Aram. form. There is also an analogy in the names of other festivals, τ. ἐγκαίνια, ἄζυμα, etc.): [[Mat.28.1|Mat.28:1]], [[Col.2.16|Col.2:16]]; ἡ ἡμέρα τῶν σ. ([[Exo.20.8|Exo.20:8]], al.), [[Luk.4.16|Luk.4:16]], [[Act.13.14; 16.13|Act.13:14 16:13]]; dative pl. (in LXX -τοις, but [[1Ma.2.38|1Ma.2:38]] as in NT) by metaplasmus (El., § 9, 3), σάββασι, [[Mat.12.1, 5; 12.10-12|Mat.12:1, 5 12:10-12]] [[Mrk.1.21; 2.23; 3.2, 4|Mrk.1:21 2:23 3:2, 4]], [[Luk.4.31; 6.2|Luk.4:31 6:2]].
2. **seven days, a week**;
(a) the sing. form: πρώτη σαββάτσυ, [[Mrk.16.9|Mrk.16:9]] δὶς τοῦ σ. (Bl., § 35, 4; 36, 13), [[Luk.18.12|Luk.18:12]] κατὰ μίαν σαββάτου, [[1Co.16.2|1Co.16:2]] pl., σ. τρία, [[Act.17.2|Act.17:2]] R, mg. (but see supr.);
(b) the pl. form: ἡ μία τῶν σ. (where the genitive = μετὰ τά; Soph., _Lex._, 43a), [[Mat.28.1|Mat.28:1]], [[Mrk.16.2|Mrk.16:2]], [[Luk.24.1|Luk.24:1]], [[Jhn.20.1, 19|Jhn.20:1, 19]], [[Act.20.7|Act.20:7]]
(AS)

G4540.def:
**Σαμαρία** (Rec. -άρεια), -ας, ἡ (Heb. שֹׁמְרוֹן; Aram. שָׁמְרַיִן),
**Samaria**;
(a) **the city**: [[Act.8.5|Act.8:5]] (and perhaps also [[Act.8.9, 14|Act.8:9, 14]]);
(b) **the region**: [[Luk.17.11|Luk.17:11]], [[Jhn.4.4-5|Jhn.4:4-5]], 7, [[Act.1.8; 8.1|Act.1:8 8:1]] (and perhaps also [[Act.8.9, 14|Act.8:9, 14]]) [[Act.9.31; 15.3|Act.9:31 15:3]].†
(AS)

G4575.def:
**σεβαστός**, -ή, -όν (σεβάζομαι)
1. reverend, august.
2. In late writers, with reference to **the Roman Imperial name**;
(a) ὁ Σ., Augustus, i.e. the Roman Emperor: [[Act.25.21, 25|Act.25:21, 25]];
(b) **Augustan**: σπείρα σ., [[Act.27.1|Act.27:1]] (See further, Deiss., BS, 218.) †
(AS)
